ns.WhatsNew = {
    { version = "6.10.1", text = "A quick fix for the error spam some of you hit after 6.10, mostly in Gnomeregan.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Party and raid frames: the |cffffffffDispel Highlight|r pulse no longer floods the error log in fights.\n      - It came from debuffs the game keeps hidden from addons, as on some Gnomeregan mobs.\n• Buffs & Debuffs: the weapon enchant row no longer causes errors in combat.\n      - When the game hides your buffs from addons, the row stays where it was.\n• Quest tracker: focusing a quest in combat no longer causes a blocked-action error.\n      - The new focus is set as soon as the fight ends." },
    { version = "6.10", text = "|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating|r (not just /reload): this version adds new files.\n\nThe big tidy-up. Edit Mode dialogs now open one section at a time, in the same order on every frame, so no more scrolling through 40 rows. The settings window got the same care: a |cffffffffGeneral|r page, clearer tabs, dropdowns that look like dropdowns, and notes that tell you why something is greyed. We cut options nobody needed, merged the ones that belonged together, and added a few you asked for. Every new option starts off. Thanks to Kabaday for the help on the loot roll window!\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffEdit Mode:|r one section open at a time, and the same sections in the same order on every frame.\n• |cffffffffSettings window:|r a new |cffffffffGeneral|r page, tidier tabs, and dropdowns with a proper arrow.\n• |cffffffffLoot rolls:|r each open roll gets its own card, with Need above Greed. By Nico-Mayer.\n• |cffffffffNew options|r for vendors, resurrections, bags, the meter and tooltips. All off until you turn them on.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffBar Edge Glow|r (off), in each frame's Look section in Edit Mode: a bright line and a soft glow at the front of the health bar. It flashes when health changes.\n• |cffffffffDamage Trail|r on the Resource Bars' health bar too.\n• Works with |cffffffffSmooth Animated Bars|r: with its option for other addons' bars on, its fill shows on FlareUI's health and power bars.\n• Edit Mode samples:\n      - The |cffffffffFive-Second Rule|r spark runs across your mana bar.\n      - Rogues and druids see sample combo gems in the ring styles.\n• Party and raid frames: |cffffffffDispel Highlight|r pulses fast. In the ring styles, the portrait ring pulses too, in the debuff's colour.\n• Resource Bars: |cffffffffAbsorb Texture|r for the health bar. Its Edit Mode sample shows incoming heals and a shield.\n• Forever Style: a frame's |cffffffffScale|r is saved per Edit Mode layout.\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags & Looting|r\n• |cffffffffBank Window|r section: |cffffffffColumns|r (Default), |cffffffffGaps Between Bags|r (off) and |cffffffffTight Spacing|r (off).\n• |cffffffffCombine Empty Slots|r (off), in Bag Window: your empty slots show as one, after your items, with the number of free slots on it.\n• |cffffffffAuto Open Containers|r (off), in Tools: clams, loot bags and lockboxes you've unlocked open by themselves.\n      - Not in combat, and not at a vendor, mailbox, bank, auction house or in a trade.\n• A note at the top of the Bags tab says why the options are greyed: another bag addon, or combined bags off.\n• Works with |cffffffffSyndicator|r: pointing at your gold lists every character's gold.\n• Works with |cffffffffHide 2FA Bag Slots|r.\n\n|cffe6cc99Meters|r\n• |cffffffffReport to Chat|r, in a meter window's right-click and gear menus: your top 3, 5 or 10 to Party, Raid, Instance, Guild, a whisper, or Say in instances. After combat only.\n• |cffffffffClose Tab|r and |cffffffffClose Window|r in the same menus.\n• |cffffffffReset on Leaving a Group|r (off), in Tweaks.\n• |cffffffffPull Warning Sound|r (off), in Threat Bars: a sound as Pull Warning starts. Never while you hold the mob.\n\n|cffe6cc99Tooltips|r\n• |cffffffffHealth Bar|r in FlareUI's look: the FlareUI Forever texture in a thin border that takes the tooltip's border colour.\n      - Now a choice, on the Content tab: |cffffffffOff|r (as before), |cffffffffBelow|r the tooltip or |cffffffffInside|r it.\n\n|cffe6cc99Quality of Life|r\n• |cffffffffRepair with Guild Funds|r (off), in Vendor: Auto Repair uses your guild bank first, when your rank allows it.\n• |cffffffffAccept Resurrections|r (off), in Other: never while you or the caster is in combat.\n• |cffffffffCoordinates on the World Map|r, in Map & Mail: your coordinates and the cursor's. It's the same as Blizzard's own two options.\n\n|cffe6cc99Chat|r\n• A tab's glow takes the colour of its newest message: green for guild, blue for party, and so on.\n• Gamepad mode: Blizzard's chat tabs look like FlareUI's.\n• Works with |cffffffffMisspelled: Forever|r: its highlights stay on the words.\n\n|cffe6cc99Action Bars|r\n• |cffffffffHow Fake CM Works|r: a short note at the top of the Fake CM tab.\n• With |cffffffffSkin Action Bars|r on, a pet spell set to autocast gets a slowly pulsing gold border.\n\n|cffe6cc99Other|r\n• Battleground Objectives: a |cffffffffScale|r slider in its Edit Mode dialog.\n• Loot rolls: each roll shows your choice, your roll and who leads, plus item level and slot. By Nico-Mayer.\n• The chat preview shows item and spell link icons when you point at |cffffffffItem and Spell Icons|r. By parchinskiy.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Edit Mode|r\n• One section opens at a time. Each frame remembers the last one you opened.\n• Every unit frame, party, raid, boss and resource bar dialog uses the same sections in the same order: Size, Text, Look, Behaviour, Cast Bar, Auras, Icons, Fading.\n• Dialogs grow taller, up to about two thirds of your screen.\n• Shorter labels: |cffffffffPower Height|r, |cffffffffBackground|r, |cffffffffBar Animations|r, |cffffffffFrame Gap|r, |cffffffffGroup Gap|r, |cffffffffGroup Order|r. Search still finds the old names.\n• Party: |cffffffffPets & Targets|r section with the Pets and Party Targets choices.\n• Classic party frames: |cffffffffDispel Icons|r can sit anywhere the auras can.\n• |cffffffffPet Happiness|r is one choice: Off or where it sits.\n• The first-time hint stays until you pick a FlareUI frame.\n\n|cffe6cc99Settings window|r\n• |cffffffffGeneral|r page (was Settings), with two tabs:\n      - |cffffffffInterface:|r UI Scale, Global Font. Custom Scale and Text Scale are sliders now.\n      - |cffffffffAdvanced:|r Sync Blizz UI, Blizzard Frames (Move Any Window) and Language.\n• Move Any Window, Sync Blizz UI and UI Scale work with Quality of Life off.\n• Dropdowns lost their two side arrows and show a down arrow inside the box.\n• Fold sections with the arrow left of their title. |cffffffffReset|r shows only when something differs from its default.\n• A module that's off lists what it gives. After |cffffffffTurn On|r, a banner offers the reload it needs.\n• Pages that keep options in Edit Mode say so under their description.\n• Tabs renamed or merged:\n      - Action Bars: |cffffffffOther Bars|r (XP Bar and Hide Bars together).\n      - Chat: |cffffffffBehaviour|r. Tooltips: |cffffffffContent|r.\n      - Minimap: |cffffffffMap|r and |cffffffffAddon Buttons|r. Quest Tracker: |cffffffffLook|r and |cffffffffBehaviour|r.\n• Unit Frames › Fonts: pick a |cffffffffFrame|r to see its fonts, and |cffffffffCopy to All Frames|r.\n• Quality of Life: Convenience is now |cffffffffQuests & NPCs|r, |cffffffffMap & Mail|r and |cffffffffOther|r. The nameplate section is |cffffffffEnemy Plates|r.\n• Profiles: |cffffffffWhat a Profile Saves|r opens the page, and Reset FlareUI sits in the Profile section.\n• The setup tour offers Buff Reminders and has its own switch for Bags & Looting.\n\n|cffe6cc99Options merged|r\n• |cffffffffAutomate Quests|r (was Auto Accept Quests and Auto Turn-In Quests). If you had either one on, you get both.\n• |cffffffffCollapsible Bag Bar|r now also removes the bag bar's frame (was two options). Either one on gives you this one on.\n• |cffffffffGryphons|r in Quality of Life › Hide Clutter: |cffffffffShown|r, |cffffffffBehind Bars|r or |cffffffffHidden|r (was Hide Gryphons and Gryphons Behind Bars). |cffffffffRaid Manager|r moved there too.\n• |cffffffffSkin Item Slots|r: |cffffffffOff|r, |cffffffffThin Borders|r or |cffffffffThick Borders|r. Skinned slots always use rarity colours.\n• |cffffffffMeter Tab in the Chat|r: one dropdown. |cffffffffDisable|r (the default), |cffffffffOpen When Clicked|r, or tick |cffffffffOpen In Combat|r, |cffffffffOpen In a Group|r and |cffffffffOpen At Login|r together.\n• |cffffffffAddons in the Drawer|r: |cffffffffNone|r turns the addon button drawer off (its own switch is gone).\n• Separate Window and Threat View in Combat: turning one on turns the other off.\n\n|cffe6cc99Always on now (switches removed)|r\n• |cffffffffDamage Trail|r on every frame.\n• |cffffffffHighlight Purgeable Buffs|r, on enemy targets and boss frames.\n• |cffffffffThreat Glow|r and |cffffffffCombat Glow|r.\n• |cffffffffTimer Colour|r, |cffffffffLatency Zone|r and the spell rank on cast bars (lower ranks only, like \"R2\").\n• Quest Tracker: |cffffffffQuest Count|r, |cffffffffHide When Empty|r, |cffffffffWrap Long Text|r and |cffffffffCollapsible Zones|r.\n• Chat: link tooltips on mouseover and copyable links.\n• Meters: the |cffffffffReady Check|r and |cffffffffCountdown|r buttons.\n• Buff Reminders: |cffffffffIgnore Members Out of Range|r.\n\n|cffe6cc99Other changes|r\n• Action Bars: |cffffffffDim on Cooldown|r is part of |cffffffffStatus Colouring|r.\n• Action Bars: |cffffffffBar Scale|r is now |cffffffffButton Scale|r, in Button Appearance. Button Text joined Button Appearance.\n• Buffs & Debuffs: weapon enchants get their own row under your buffs, so every buff row lines up.\n• Meters: |cffffffffTank's Lead|r shows after the numbers, like \"100% (+25%)\".\n• Loot rolls: each roll still to decide gets its own card, with Need above Greed and Pass beside them. By Nico-Mayer.\n• Chat: Formatting's note says it only works outside dungeons, raids and battlegrounds.\n\n|cffffd100Defaults|r\n• Buffs & Debuffs › Buffs: |cffffffffSize|r 30, |cffffffffIcons per Row|r 8, |cffffffffMax Icons|r 16.\n• Meters: |cffffffffTank's Lead|r on.\n• Resource Bars: |cffffffffQueued Attack Colour|r, |cffffffffStand-Still Zone|r and |cffffffffWaiting State|r on.\n• Only settings you never changed take the new defaults.\n\n|cffffd100Removed|r\n• Quality of Life: |cffffffffFlag Carrier Frames|r and |cffffffffDurability Warning|r (Buff Reminders' Low Durability covers it).\n• Cast bars: |cffffffffChannel Ticks|r and |cffffffffSpell Queue Window|r.\n• Quest Tracker: |cffffffffFocus Buttons|r and |cffffffffAuto Quest Buttons|r. Quest Icons still focus a quest when clicked.\n• Chat: |cffffffffColon After Names|r.\n• Tooltips: |cffffffffShow Guild Ranks|r.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Target frame: a friendly target's buffs no longer show twice, once with a white border.\n• Gamepad: D-pad Up and Down work on the action bar again with the quest tracker on. The tracker list scrolls with the right stick.\n• Click-cast addons work on the player, target, focus and other single frames again.\n• Action bar 1 shows its keybinds right after logging in.\n• Quest tracker: Shift-click links a quest into any open chat box, like Whisper Messenger's. By parchinskiy.\n• Action bars: a stance, pet or possess bar left 1 pixel wide is sized again, so Edit Mode can select it.\n• Chat: tab glow works again.\n• Gamepad mode: the chat tabs are no longer dim and fade with the chat.\n• Settings: lists only make room for a scrollbar when they need one. By parchinskiy.\n• Settings: the Bags & Looting preview shows the search box, sort button and Category Filters. By parchinskiy.\n\n|cffffd100Translations|r\n• French: the 6.9 text. By Braincell1980." },
    { version = "6.9", text = "Version 6.9. (Nice!) All your fading now lives in Edit Mode. The chat, the Damage Meter and the threat window can join fade groups at last, every Visibility list learns |cffffffffIn an Instance|r, and Edit Mode's settings open right next to the frame you clicked. Also new: Chinese, by AreChen, and a pile of quest tracker and chat options you asked for.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffFading in Edit Mode:|r the chat, the Damage Meter and the threat window get a |cffffffffFading|r section in Edit Mode, like every other frame. They can join fade groups.\n• |cffffffffEdit Mode settings open next to the frame you select|r, and stay on screen.\n• |cffffffffIn an Instance|r on every Visibility list.\n• |cffffffffChinese:|r Simplified and Traditional Chinese, by AreChen.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Chat|r\n• |cffffffffTab Sets Channel|r (off), in Chat › Tweaks: clicking a tab that shows only one kind of chat, like Guild or Party, makes it the kind you type in.\n      - It goes by what the tab shows, not its name.\n      - A tab that shows several kinds keeps your current one. Party or Raid when you're not in one: Say.\n\n|cffe6cc99Quest Tracker|r\n• |cffffffffQuest Icons|r (off), in Display: Blizzard's round icons before each quest, \"…\" while in progress and \"?\" when ready to turn in. Click one to focus the quest.\n• |cffffffffShow Complete Tag|r (on), in Display: turn it off and finished quests lose \"(Complete)\" and the green colour.\n• |cffffffffShow Untracked Quests|r (off), in Quests: with zone headings, quests in your zone that you don't track show too, dimmed. Shift-click one to track it.\n• |cffffffffCollapsible Zones|r (on), in Quests: click a zone heading to fold its quests. The heading now shows Blizzard's fold arrow.\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags & Looting|r\n• |cffffffffCombined Backpack|r, in Bag Window: the same as Blizzard's |cffffffffUse Combined Bags|r. The options below it need it on.\n• |cffffffffSort Bags on Open|r (off), in Tools: your bags tidy themselves each time you open them, as the broom button does. Not in a fight, and not at a vendor, the mailbox, the bank, the auction house or a trade. By ronborens.\n\n|cffe6cc99Buff Reminders|r\n• Paladins: right-click the aura reminder for |cffffffffAura to Cast|r: |cffffffffLast Used|r (the default) or one aura.\n• Elixirs, in Reminders › Consumables, by GregDuhamel from Celbrund's idea:\n      - |cffffffffElixirs to Watch|r: |cffffffffTicked Ones|r (as before) or |cffffffffThose in Your Bags|r, every elixir you carry with nothing to tick.\n      - |cffffffffElixirs to Keep Up|r: |cffffffffEach of Them|r (as before) or |cffffffffAny One of Them|r, one icon until any of them is on you.\n      - Lower ranks of an elixir count, and a click drinks the best one you carry.\n      - The flask reminder can be clicked to drink your flask.\n\n|cffe6cc99Quality of Life|r\n• |cffffffffBetter Camera|r is now two sliders in Gameplay: |cffffffffMax Zoom|r and |cffffffffZoom Speed|r.\n      - Both start at Blizzard's own values. If you had Better Camera on, you keep its values.\n      - Zoom Speed is greyed in Gamepad mode.\n\n|cffe6cc99Player Cast Bar|r\n• Its |cffffffffVisibility|r in Edit Mode has |cffffffffNever|r: it hides FlareUI's cast bar and keeps Blizzard's hidden too, so only the player frame's own Cast Bar shows.\n\n|cffe6cc99Translations|r\n• |cffffffffSimplified Chinese|r and |cffffffffTraditional Chinese|r, by AreChen. Pick them in Settings › Language.\n• French: all the 6.8.1 and 6.8.2 text, by Braincell1980.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Fading|r\n• The chat's, the Damage Meter's and the threat window's fading options moved from the settings window to Edit Mode. Your choices carry over.\n      - The chat's Visibility has a new |cffffffffNew Messages|r choice: a new line, or closing a quest or vendor window, brings it back. Typing always shows the chat.\n      - The chat and the meter have a |cffffffffFade Delay|r: how long they stay before fading.\n      - The meter's Visibility has |cffffffffNever|r (the old Hidden). Its Show on Mouseover is now the Mouseover choice.\n      - The threat window starts on |cffffffffSame as Meter|r, as before.\n      - The Chat and Meters pages have a |cffffffffFading in Edit Mode|r button.\n• Every Visibility list has |cffffffffIn an Instance|r, under In a Group.\n• |cffffffffHas an Attackable Target|r is now |cffffffffAttackable Target|r.\n• |cffffffffFade In Speed|r and |cffffffffFade Out Speed|r are now |cffffffffShow Speed|r and |cffffffffHide Speed|r.\n\n|cffe6cc99Edit Mode|r\n• The settings dialog opens next to the frame you select, not in a corner of the screen. FlareUI's own Fading box stays right under Blizzard's dialog, on screen.\n• Fading sections open and close, and start closed, on every frame.\n• The Damage Meter's dialog no longer shows |cffffffffText Size|r. The meter's fonts are in Meters › Fonts.\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffFull Player Names|r now works on party frames in every style. The focus frame always shows first names.\n• FlareUI Style: the portrait ring is a softer bronze, closer to the frame's border.\n\n|cffe6cc99Other|r\n• |cffffffffNameplate Font|r also sets the names over characters in the world. They change after a full restart of the game.\n• The hunter pet reminder stays quiet with the |cffffffffLone Wolf|r talent.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Bags: you can right-click items again after opening the bags through the crafting bag icon in a fight. By parchinskiy.\n• Damage Meter: closing Edit Mode no longer shows an error. By tinker-n-tailor.\n• Fonts: a font from another addon, like SharedMedia, applies even when that addon loads after FlareUI.\n• Settings window: small buttons no longer grow when you point at them." },
    { version = "6.8.2", text = "A round of fixes from your reports: chat tabs you can see in Gamepad mode, no more reload prompts when you switch to an alt, and two small options from the general chat.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags & Looting|r\n• Bag Window: |cffffffffCombined Backpack|r, the same as Blizzard's |cffffffffUse Combined Bags|r.\n      - The options below it need it on, so you no longer have to find Blizzard's option to use them.\n\n|cffe6cc99Player Cast Bar|r\n• Its |cffffffffVisibility|r in Edit Mode has a new |cffffffffNever|r choice.\n      - It hides FlareUI's cast bar and keeps Blizzard's hidden too, so only the player frame's own |cffffffffCast Bar|r shows.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Chat|r\n• Gamepad mode: the chat tabs stay fully visible. They faded out each time the controller left the chat.\n\n|cffe6cc99Sync Blizz UI|r\n• Switching from your main to an alt no longer asks for a reload when nothing changed.\n      - An alt only copies settings your main really changed.\n      - It only asks for a reload when one of those needs it.\n\n|cffe6cc99Buff Reminders|r\n• Fortitude: a player with Forever's |cffffffffFirst Aid Kit|r buff from a campfire counts as having it. The two can't stack.\n• A new custom reminder shows in the settings list right away.\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffHighlight Purgeable Buffs|r only applies to enemies. A friendly target's buffs show normally, with no white border.\n\n|cffe6cc99Other|r\n• Flight Timer: a route timed for the first time reads |cffffffffNew Route|r and counts up. It used to say \"Learning\".\n• Quest Tracker: \"(Complete)\" uses the game's own word in languages FlareUI isn't translated into yet." },
    { version = "6.8.1", text = "A quick follow-up to 6.8: the Damage Meter settings open again, party frames show the debuffs you can dispel, and paladins pick which aura the reminder casts.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Buff Reminders|r\n• Right-click the paladin aura reminder for |cffffffffAura to Cast|r.\n      - |cffffffffLast Used|r (the default): a click casts the last aura you had up, such as Retribution or Concentration after you die.\n      - Or pick one aura to always cast: Devotion, Retribution, Concentration, a resistance aura or Sanctity.\n• Custom reminders: type a food's or potion's name while it's in your bags, and the reminder gets its icon and a click uses it.\n      - To track a food's buff, add the buff's name too, for example |cffffd100item:4593, Well Fed|r.\n\n|cffe6cc99Translations|r\n• French: all the 6.8 text is translated. By Braincell1980.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Damage Meter|r\n• The Damage Meter settings page opens again. 6.8 showed an error there.\n• A meter window on its own no longer gets its Threat tab back.\n\n|cffe6cc99Party and Raid Frames|r\n• Debuffs you can dispel show in your |cffffffffDebuffs|r place again while |cffffffffDispel Icons|r are on.\n      - Before, they only showed as the small type symbol in the middle of the bar.\n      - This affected every party style, the raid frames and the main tank frames." },
}
